# Line endings that matter, pinned so a checkout cannot change behaviour.
#
# cmd.exe's parser mishandles a .bat whose lines end LF-only: multi-line ( ... )
# blocks and goto/label jumps are the documented failure cases. A launcher can
# therefore work on the machine it was written on and fail only for somebody who
# cloned it - the hardest kind of bug to hear about, because the reporter has no
# way to see what changed. Pinning it here stops an editor, a zip round-trip or a
# `git checkout` from silently "normalising" them.

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
